                    {
                        "description": "ergoemacs paragraphs: left cmd + 8 down a paragraph, 9 up. Left key down, right key up, which is the way round c and v had it before. They were on c and v, and that cost cmd+c and cmd+v -- the two shortcuts with the strongest muscle memory on the machine -- and worse, made them scroll: what they emit is option+arrow, and firefox and telegram read that as scrolling rather than as a paragraph move. Digits are not system shortcuts on macOS, cmd+1 to cmd+9 being left to applications; the one real loss is that a browser puts tab N on cmd+1 to cmd+8 and the last tab on cmd+9. Left cmd only, as everywhere here, so right cmd keeps both.",
