                    {
                        "description": "ergoemacs kill line: left cmd + g kills to end of line, G to the start. G is cmd+delete, which is a real native combo; g is ctrl+k, which cocoa text fields understand. g reaches terminals as well, because ctrl+k is already kill-line in zsh and kill-to-end-of-line in Claude Code -- it is the one control key here that collides with nothing, unlike ctrl+a, which is the tmux prefix in .tmux.conf. G does not: cmd+delete is not something a terminal can send, and the alternative would be ctrl+u, which zsh binds to kill-whole-line rather than backward-kill-line. So G keeps going through the terminal rule and does nothing there.",
